  "articleBody": "Sometimes a DIY fix for your mobile home door or trim is all you need, but other times, it's definitely best to call in a professional. Here are the signs that it's time to get some help: \n*   **Structural Framing Issues:** If the problem seems to go beyond the door itself and involves the surrounding structural framing, that's a job for an expert. \n*   **Exterior Door Replacement:** Replacing an exterior door in a mobile home can be more complex than an interior one, especially when you need to ensure proper sealing and security. \n*   **Major Water Damage:** If you're seeing significant water damage around the door or trim, it's crucial to address the source of the leak and repair the damage correctly to prevent future issues. \n*   **Repeated Fit/Alignment Failures:** If you've tried all the simple fixes—tightening hinges, sanding, replacing weatherstripping—and the door still won't cooperate, it might indicate a larger opening problem that needs a professional assessment. \n*   **Uncertainty About the Cause:** If you're just not sure why your door isn't working right, a professional can quickly diagnose the problem and offer the right solution. Don't hesitate to reach out if you're in doubt!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
